+    <section class="bs"><div class="bs-h"><h2>01 &middot; The brief</h2><p>Applewise Bakery is a Scottish institution - rooted in Stirling, built on family heritage, and famous for its apple pies. But the brief wasn't about celebrating what they had. It was about making sure what they looked like matched what they stood for.</p></div><div class="bp"><div class="bp-t"><div class="bp-k">What they asked for</div><h3>A refreshed identity that told the whole story.</h3><p>Applewise had the heritage, the product, and the artisan values. The brief was to bring all of it forward - Scottish roots, handcrafted quality, the apple pies they were famous for. Everything, visible, in one place.</p><div class="bp-k">What it really meant</div><h3>Don't include everything. Find the one thing.</h3><p>The real challenge wasn't how to show more - it was how to reduce. A stronger identity wouldn't come from accumulation. It would come from finding the single idea that contained everything else.</p></div><div class="bpc-stack"><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery brand identity design" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/7vNDUzbrfopnDHf2KrhNBcIjFVs.jpg"/></figure></div></div></section>
+    <section class="bs"><div class="bs-h"><h2>02 &middot; The direction</h2><p>The routes I ruled out, and the one I chose.</p></div><div class="bp"><div class="bp-t"><div class="bp-k" style="color:var(--muted)">Ruled out</div><h3>Five directions. Five dead ends.</h3><p>Five routes were explored in full. Heritage-led (tartan shield, Scottish crest) communicated origin but buried the product. Product-led (illustrated pie) was clear but flat - nothing to make it stick. Craft aesthetics (rolling pins, wheat, rustic type) felt borrowed. Combining everything - tartan, pie, thistle, apple - answered the brief literally and failed it creatively. A modern minimal mark was clean but had no story. Each direction worked on its own terms. None unified the brand.</p><div class="bp-k">Chosen</div><h3>Two ideas. One mark.</h3><p>The apple pie lattice and the MacLeod tartan share the same underlying geometry - a repeating grid of interlocking lines. Overlaid, they don't compete: they become one cohesive form. Product and heritage, resolved into a single mark that needs no explanation, but rewards the eye. The answer wasn't to include more. It was to find where two things were already the same thing.</p></div><div class="bpc-stack"><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery logo and packaging design" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/BXfHsHGXofbU2z2xJzE2MxBgWuM.jpg"/></figure></div></div></section>
+    <section class="bs"><div class="bs-h"><h2>03 &middot; The system</h2><p>Combining the lattice pattern from the top of a traditional apple pie with the MacLeod tartan produced something that was immediately distinctive and deeply meaningful - a logo that doesn't need explaining, but rewards those who look closer.</p></div><div class="bpc-g c2"><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/6nESDu3a3NTMbPFVigq5n6cVYlY.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/Nj3XzFKDR1oOzeT04JTsuiikaE4.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/z0LPUnwZP9TJ3Rtz9p3UOtq5oc.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/IESDyiApBk4kvyvVamQnToTJlaU.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/nHaroksfEgS986LsvYAcTjUeyQ.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/r3ElifG6wUylRtgDr1FQQFldsI.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/vLrq1CYGi5tknHbriU9cwCWB4s.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/NqFEpQCHJSsOAZ2IVqUF20VWoc.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery project image" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/YJSqIfI94SBD2WsRF6CIkHa0.gif"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery logo variations" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/3BDBKgUbvdfSwFh8PFGvZ2VRh1Q.jpg"/></figure><figure class="bpc-f"><img alt="Applewise Bakery storefront branding Scotland" loading="lazy" onclick="openLightbox(this.src)" src="https://framerusercontent.com/modules/iZzbvuOgImdAjKy2dnTK/Si0Nc0VxZgYlBpVB9Xt3/assets/6ROo1JxtoLXn6LTqCy9mm1yf9Q.jpg"/></figure></div></section>
+    <div class="proc-call" style="border-radius:var(--r);margin-bottom:96px;"><div class="proc-call-bg">"</div><div class="proc-call-tag">The Call</div><div class="proc-call-quote">The brief asked for everything. The mark says it <em>all</em> - in one shape.</div><p class="proc-call-body">Five directions explored, each capturing something real. The answer came from stopping the accumulation and asking a different question: not what to include, but where two things were already the same thing. The lattice was always the tartan. The tartan was always the pie.</p></div>
